# U-Boot environment variable access configuration for fw_printenv / fw_setenv.
#
# For Raspberry Pi 5 the U-Boot environment lives in a raw FAT file on the
# boot partition rather than in a dedicated MTD device.
#
# Format: <device>   <offset>  <env-size>  <flash-sector-size>
#
# The offset 0x0000 means the environment is stored as a plain file named
# "uboot.env" in the FAT filesystem; libubootenv handles this transparently
# when the path ends with a file extension.
#
# If your build uses a raw SD/eMMC offset, replace with:
#   /dev/mmcblk0  0x3F000  0x1000  0x1000
/boot/uboot.env  0x0000  0x4000  0x4000
